# Persofi Future Enhancements

## Product Goal

Make Persofi easy enough to use consistently. Capturing a normal expense should take seconds, and importing a receipt should produce a trustworthy draft that only needs review and confirmation.

## Product Principles

- Optimize for one person using the application locally.
- Reduce data-entry effort before adding more reporting features.
- Keep manual transaction entry available and fast.
- Treat AI output as an editable draft, never as confirmed financial data.
- Validate amounts with deterministic calculations rather than AI confidence.
- Learn store and product mappings from confirmed corrections.
- Allow an item to remain unmapped when receipt text is ambiguous.
- Preserve backups and data integrity even though advanced security is not a priority.

## Priority 0 - Transaction Entry Usability

### Quick Manual Entry

- Provide two clear entry paths: Scan Receipt and Manual Entry.
- Replace the large nested transaction/item dialogs with a focused entry workspace.
- Default the date to today and remember the most recently used account and person.
- Suggest recently used stores and accounts first.
- Allow a simple expense with account, store, total, tax, and optional category.
- Make itemization optional for manual expenses.
- Edit item descriptions, quantities, prices, categories, and product mappings inline.
- Support keyboard navigation and automatic focus for repeated entry.
- Add Save Draft and Save & Process actions.
- Preserve manual entry for income, transfer, credit payment, and refund transactions.
- Show actionable validation and API errors in the interface.

### Transaction List

- Show newest transactions first.
- Load recent transactions by default and paginate older history.
- Add filters for date, transaction type, account type, store, person, and status.
- Make unprocessed drafts easy to find and resume.
- Provide a clear duplicate warning before saving likely duplicate expenses.

## Priority 1 - Receipt-Assisted Entry

### Receipt Capture and Extraction

- Accept receipt photos and PDFs from desktop or mobile camera upload.
- Correct common image orientation and quality problems before extraction.
- Extract merchant name, date, currency, subtotal, tax, discounts, fees, total, and line items.
- Return structured extraction results through a provider-independent backend interface.
- Start with a hosted vision model for the first implementation.
- Keep a local OCR provider as a future option if cost, privacy, or availability becomes a concern.
- Keep AI credentials exclusively on the backend.

### Review and Validation

- Display the receipt beside an editable transaction draft.
- Highlight uncertain, missing, inconsistent, and unmapped fields.
- Verify quantity multiplied by unit price against each line total.
- Verify item totals and adjustments against the subtotal.
- Verify subtotal plus tax and fees against the receipt total.
- Require account selection and user confirmation before processing.
- Never automatically save and process a transaction directly from AI output.
- Detect likely duplicate receipts using image hash, store, date, and total.
- Permit confirmation only when required fields and arithmetic checks pass.

### Store and Product Mapping Memory

- Map normalized merchant text to an existing Persofi store.
- Map receipt item text, scoped by store where possible, to product variants, categories, and brands.
- Prefer previously confirmed aliases over fuzzy or AI suggestions.
- Present ranked candidates when no confirmed mapping exists.
- Remember corrections after a transaction is confirmed.
- Allow explicit creation of a new store, product, or variant during review.
- Allow unresolved items to retain their raw description without a product mapping.

## Priority 2 - Reliability and Performance

- Use one shared Prisma client and connection pool.
- Use decimal-safe or epsilon-based monetary validation.
- Make transaction creation and processing an atomic backend operation.
- Prevent accidental modification or deletion of processed transactions.
- Add query caching for accounts, stores, people, categories, products, and brands.
- Avoid refetching the complete transaction history after every mutation.
- Add server-side filtering and pagination to growing transaction and balance endpoints.
- Add an endpoint for latest balances by account.
- Improve loading, empty, retry, and failure states.
- Add focused tests for manual entry, extraction validation, mapping, duplicates, and processing.

## Priority 3 - Data Ownership

- Keep full database export and restore support.
- Add receipt-import metadata to backups.
- Make receipt image retention configurable.
- Default to deleting a receipt image after confirmation while retaining extracted text and mappings.
- Document recovery steps and verify backup compatibility after schema changes.

## Priority 4 - Reporting and Convenience

- Historical balances grouped by account type.
- Monthly expense versus income chart.
- Expense split by credit versus debit account type.
- Expense grouped by parent category.
- Tax paid total and tax history.
- Historical net worth chart.
- CSV transaction export.
- Monthly budget envelopes and budget-versus-actual reporting.

## Deferred / Not Planned Initially

- Authentication, authorization, and multi-user support.
- Enterprise-grade security hardening.
- Fully autonomous receipt ingestion without review.
- Training a custom OCR or receipt model before evaluating an off-the-shelf provider.
- Additional dashboard work before transaction entry is demonstrably easier.
